.TITLE "umount"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Unmounts filesystems. It detaches a __storage device__ or network share from the system hierarchy, ensuring all data is written before removal.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**umount mount_point**
Unmounts a filesystem from a specific directory or volume.
> __mount_point__ the target path or volume

**umount /dev/disk2s1**
Unmounts a filesystem by specifying its device path.
> __/dev/disk2s1__ the device path

**umount -f mount_point**
Forcefully unmounts a filesystem even if it is currently in use.
> __-f__ force flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Always attempt to unmount a drive normally before using the __-f__ flag. Forcefully unmounting a device that is still being written to can result in __data corruption__ and should be handled with care.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:mount** **mac:diskutil**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/umount.html__
